WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:07.360
There's something timeless and romantic about
living on the ragged edge of civilization.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.780
Whether you prefer the American Old West,
the final frontier of space, or somewhere

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:17.050
in between, the thought of living in roguish
freedom is certainly appealing to many.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.190
If you are hoping to find somewhere free from
the shackles of laws in our world today, here

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:28.340
are some places you might want to investigate.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:34.800
On the border between Afghanistan and Pakistan
sits an area known as Ungoverned Afghanistan

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.270
and it is just that, ungoverned, at least
to some extent.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.210
More officially know as The Federally Administered
Tribal Areas, it provides a great opportunity

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:48.400
to experience all the danger and thrills of
the Old West in the modern era.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.820
While officially under the jurisdiction of
Pakistan’s federal government, the areas

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.390
are considered “semi-autonomous”, which
means that they are bound more by tribal laws

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.150
than the Frontier Crimes Regulations that
Pakistan has put over them.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.579
Basically the law of the land is whatever
the local tribes and warlords make it out

00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:06.579
to be.

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:10.429
When the Supreme Court of Pakistan refuses
to deal with the region, you just know it’s

00:01:10.429 --> 00:01:11.979
a dodgy area.

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:17.899
Seven tribal districts, also known as agencies,
divide the land with six frontier regions.

00:01:17.899 --> 00:01:22.700
Though they are represented in the Parliament
of Pakistan by elected representatives, the

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.780
tribal districts have no problem with rejecting
Parliamentary resolutions they don’t approve

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:28.780
of.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.560
Surprisingly, support for the Pakistani military
is high among the tribes, with nearly eighty

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.270
percent approving of an eventual military
government.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:42.210
For now, the Federally Administered Tribal
Areas remain a hotbed of militant activity,

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:47.420
thanks in no small part to the lack of control
Pakistan wields over the region.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:51.999
If you fancy rubbing shoulders with outlaws,
brigands and warlords then be sure to book

00:01:51.999 --> 00:01:53.840
the next available flight.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.840
If sand dunes and open spaces are more to
your liking, then you’re going to love the

00:01:58.840 --> 00:01:59.880
Western Sahara.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:05.499
It has the honor of being one of the most
sparsely populated territories in the world,

00:02:05.499 --> 00:02:10.220
with around two people per square kilometer,
based on best estimates.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:14.810
With all that space, it’s simply a daunting
prospect for any one government to control

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:15.810
it.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:20.200
The Western Sahara region was considered a
Spanish colony until the late 20th century,

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:25.290
after which Morocco and Mauritania fought
with the native Sahrawi people for the right

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.500
to the land.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:32.820
Mauritania soon gave up, leaving Morocco to
claim the most valuable portions while the

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.710
Sahrawi were left with vast tracts of barren
desert.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:42.190
Despite Morocco’s tenuous grasp on the region,
the United Nations refuses to recognize their

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:43.190
claim.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:46.470
Instead, they consider the Western Sahara
to be a “non-self-governing territory”

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:52.480
due to the question of whether Spain had adequately
“decolonized” it when they cut ties and

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.480
left.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:58.360
For now, if you’re interested in herding
camels with the Sahrawi and hiding among the

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:03.490
dunes, it seems that no one knows what laws
actually apply to the area or how to enforce

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.490
them.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:07.340
Best to take advantage of the situation whilst
it lasts.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:11.060
If you were to commit a crime out there the
locals wouldn’t even know who to report

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.670
you to, never mind prosecution.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:18.400
With the region’s lack of laws mainly attributed
to political negligence and a general mindset

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:23.510
of “wow this area’s so large and unpopulated
who actually gives a toss.”

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.660
I imagine you could probably get away with
quite a lot in this vast expanse of barren

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:28.770
dessert.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.810
If living the pirate’s life on the high
seas appeals to you, grab yourself a boat

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.180
and head out to international waters.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:42.040
Territorial waters for any nation only extends
twenty-two kilometers out from the shore,

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:52.580
you aren’t truly free until you move through
the contiguous zone, which extends another

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.040
twenty-two kilometers beyond.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:02.770
And even then, if you’re caught engaging
in egregious acts of piracy, any nation has

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.410
the ability to bring you to justice.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.790
But there’s a whole lot of water out there.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:10.670
Unless you attract an awful lot of attention
to yourself, you’re just another speck on

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:11.670
the horizon.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.140
There’s something magical about the high
seas.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:18.239
Since the very first ships, the idea of sailing
the open ocean has inspired generations of

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:22.510
artists, spawning beautiful paintings, books,
and even movies.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:28.040
To apply laws to such an unruly stretch of
water would almost be an insult to what is

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.320
one of Earth’s last true remaining wildernesses.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.940
International waters are regulated out of
necessity in our modern world, but enforcing

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:40.240
the rules is an impossible task for the world’s
governments.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:46.430
Thus, the world’s oceans remain one of the
last truly lawless places on Earth.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:52.139
As the great Hugo Grotius said in the early
seventeenth century, people from all nations

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:54.810
have a right to the waterways of the world.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:05:00.720
He called this right Mare Liberum, Latin for
“The Free Sea”, and his book by the same

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.710
name laid the groundwork for the concept of
international waters, as we know them today.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:11.810
So set sail for the high seas, and celebrate
the freedom Grotius championed centuries past.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:17.750
In January of 1991, Somalia suddenly found
its central government dissolved as it plunged

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:21.780
into a bloody civil war that still rages on
to this day.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:26.570
In the two decades that followed anarchy ruled
the day, as warlords fought among themselves

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:30.950
for the opportunity to rule small sections
of the fragmented country.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:35.700
There have since been several attempts to
reestablish order in the region, starting

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:40.690
with the short-lived Transitional National
Government in 2000, and most recently with

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:44.670
the Federal Government of Somalia in 2012.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:49.010
Only time will tell whether the latter is
effective, though the formation of a parliament

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:53.560
and election of an official president lends
some momentum to the effort.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.400
Meanwhile, the region remains fractured.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:00.930
The concept of government is only half the
battle in a world of militants and local rule,

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.950
where might makes right when it comes to the
law.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:09.280
And in the Internet Age, it’s hard to gain
credibility when there are multiple web pages

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.639
all claiming to represent your fledgling government.

00:06:12.639 --> 00:06:14.930
Piracy is a major problem in Somalia.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:20.081
With basically no laws or enforcement agencies
to keep a lid on things, pirates rule the

00:06:20.081 --> 00:06:25.210
high seas around the country, making the waters
surrounding Somalia one of the most dangerous

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.920
shipping routes in the world.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:32.370
In 1923, the British government decided to
grant New Zealand their own little piece of

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.120
the ice-encrusted Antarctic wasteland.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.820
They established the Ross Dependency, New
Zealand’s own little cheese-shaped triangle

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:41.120
of Antarctica.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:45.540
Which included a swath of the continent and
also extended out into the sea to cover a

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.630
small archipelago known as the Balleny Islands.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:52.520
To date, New Zealand hasn’t quite figured
out what to do with them.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:56.630
There has been no attempt thus far to establish
a colony on the islands.

00:06:56.630 --> 00:07:00.970
Though still technically under the governance
of New Zealand, if there is a bright center

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:05.740
to civilization then the Balleny Islands are
certainly far from it.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:10.449
Though the Antarctica Act of 1960 established
a precedent for prosecuting criminal acts

00:07:10.449 --> 00:07:15.320
in the Ross Dependency, it doesn’t seem
anyone is willing to make the trip to actually

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:16.840
enforce the law.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:21.770
The closest anyone in New Zealand has come
to acknowledging the Balleny Islands’ existence

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:26.910
directly was a proposal to establish them
as a marine preserve in May of 1999.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:31.290
That’s pretty much the equivalent of saying,
“Well, we can’t quite figure out what

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:32.290
to do with them.

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:36.050
Perhaps we should just leave them to the penguins
and fish.”

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:41.370
Even within the United States, there are certain
places that escape the roving eye of the law.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:47.310
Located in an arid expanse of the Sonoran
desert in Southern California, Slab City is

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:52.630
one such place, where people go when they
really want to get away from it all.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:56.570
Officially the site is owned by the State
of California, though it is small and desolate

00:07:56.570 --> 00:07:59.810
enough to avoid close scrutiny by the government.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:04.610
Built on the remnants of an old military barracks,
Slab City is named for the large concrete

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:07.050
slabs left behind after the barracks was demolished.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:13.210
Most of the residents live in RVs, campers,
and tents, amidst shanty structures that serve

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:16.930
as meeting places for music and community
gatherings.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:21.830
Though they purchase most of their supplies
from a nearby town, the “slabbers” pride

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:27.250
themselves on their self-sufficiency, choosing
to go without many modern luxuries in exchange

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.470
for the freedom Slab City offers.

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:35.839
Called “the last free place on earth”
by its inhabitants, the population of mostly

00:08:35.839 --> 00:08:40.250
hippies and plain old weirdo’s fluctuates
with the seasons.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:46.490
From the one hundred and fifty or so permanent
residents, to nearly two thousand people during

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:48.130
peak months.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:53.550
Some are attracted to the weather—others,
the isolation—but all enjoy the rare opportunity

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:58.230
to experience a lifestyle free from the burden
of regulation and rules.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:02.420
Free, at least, until the State of California
demands the land back.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:08.300
Last, but certainly not least, is Pitcairn
Island in the Southern Pacific Ocean.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:14.890
With a population of only forty-eight people
as of a July 2014 estimate, it is the smallest

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:18.470
national jurisdiction in the world by population.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:23.350
On an island of only forty-seven square kilometers,
that means there isn’t much room to spread

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:27.230
your legs—you’d better hope you don’t
make any enemies whilst you’re there.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:32.390
Pitcairn Island, and the unpopulated islands
around it, are claimed as a British Overseas

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:34.550
Territory by the United Kingdom.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.870
Because we all know how much the UK just loves
to stick flags into things and say it’s

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:39.870
theirs.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:43.250
Though the residents of Pitcairn Island bend
their knees to the crown ruler, they’ve

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:48.630
been allowed to establish a local parliament
to handle matters on the island via representative

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:49.630
democracy.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:55.020
Essentially, the islanders are left alone
to craft their own laws and self-govern, as

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:57.970
long as the Queen can peek over their shoulder
now and then.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:02.310
Despite Britain’s claim to Pitcairn Island
and its surrounds, the United Nations still

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:05.650
considers the area to be a non-self-governing
territory.

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:10.700
With so few people involved in the democratic
process, it must be difficult to cast votes

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:11.700
objectively.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:38.060
Vote for the wrong person, and you just might
have your dinner burned that night.

